-- TMF Community Support System - M2 "Database ready" seed (01 auth users)
-- Generated by /workspace/tmf/seed/gen/build.py. All seed ids match the LIKE pattern
--   '5eed____-5eed-4eed-8eed-5eed5eed5eed'  and all seed auth emails match 'seed.%@example.com'.
-- Run order: 01_seed_auth_users.sql -> 02_seed.sql -> 03_seed_verify.sql ; cleanup: 04_seed_cleanup.sql
--
-- Creates 42 confirmed email/password test accounts directly in auth.users + auth.identities
-- (columns as Supabase Auth expects them: token columns '' not NULL, bcrypt hash, provider 'email').
-- 14 login accounts (2 administrators + 3 per other role) get the test password; the other 28
-- are data-only (encrypted_password = '') and cannot sign in with a password.
-- Side effects (existing triggers, by design):
--   on_auth_user_created -> handle_new_user(): profiles row (account_status 'pending', role from
--     metadata; 'administrator' is downgraded to 'beneficiary') + the matching role profile;
--   create_user_settings_after_profile_insert -> user_settings row with defaults.
--   02_seed.sql then activates the accounts and promotes the 2 administrators.
-- PASSWORD: replace __SET_TEST_PASSWORD_HERE__ below in the SQL Editor ONLY, run, then close the tab
-- without saving. Never commit a real value. If the placeholder is left in, the script aborts.
-- Idempotent: re-running skips seed users that already exist (on conflict do nothing).
